From: Nick Schuetz <nschuetz@redhat.com>
Subject: [PATCH] BuiltInPackages: gate Stage 1 system-library swaps for Linux distro packagers

Stage 1 of the Fedora-inclusion roadmap (BUNDLED_LIBRARIES.md) migrates
each `ly_associate_package` entry that has a clean Fedora equivalent
from the upstream packages.o3de.org CDN to the system package. This
patch establishes the convention used by all Stage 1 swaps: each
migrated package is wrapped in an `if (NOT LY_USE_SYSTEM_<X>) ... else()
... endif()` gate. Setting `-DLY_USE_SYSTEM_<X>=ON` (which the o3de-rpm
spec does in %build when the matching `system_<lib>` bcond is enabled)
skips the upstream fetcher and falls through to cmake's standard
find_package() pathway. The else-branch additionally aliases the system
target into the `3rdParty::<name>` namespace O3DE consumers expect.

Each gate is independent of the others — packagers can opt one bundle
at a time onto the system version without touching the rest. Default
(both flags absent) preserves upstream behavior 100%.

Currently gated:

  - LY_USE_SYSTEM_EXPAT     → cmake's stock FindEXPAT, EXPAT::EXPAT
  - LY_USE_SYSTEM_TIFF      → cmake's stock FindTIFF, TIFF::TIFF
  - LY_USE_SYSTEM_FREETYPE  → cmake's stock FindFreetype, Freetype::Freetype
  - LY_USE_SYSTEM_LUA       → cmake's stock FindLua, Lua::Lua
  - LY_USE_SYSTEM_MIKKELSEN → companion sources/Findmikkelsen-system.cmake
                              (mikkelsen has no cmake-stock find module;
                              the find module locates system mikktspace
                              and bridges its include path)
  - LY_USE_SYSTEM_PNG       → cmake's stock FindPNG, PNG::PNG
  - LY_USE_SYSTEM_ZLIB      → cmake's stock FindZLIB, ZLIB::ZLIB

Future migrations follow the same pattern. The else-branch's alias is
guarded by `if (NOT TARGET 3rdParty::<name>)` so that bundled find
modules (which create the alias themselves when downloaded) don't
collide on a mixed-mode build.

The else-branch's find_package call is load-bearing: gating out
`ly_associate_package` without replacing it means nothing ever triggers
find_package, the target never gets created, and consumers silently
link nothing. Discovered the hard way on build 10418378 (mikkelsen-only
gate without else-branch — Tier 2 swap-consistency test caught it).

---
--- a/cmake/3rdParty/Platform/Linux/BuiltInPackages_linux_x86_64.cmake	2026-05-03 06:51:31.161046526 -0500
+++ b/cmake/3rdParty/Platform/Linux/BuiltInPackages_linux_x86_64.cmake	2026-05-03 06:51:31.161814105 -0500
@@ -17,17 +17,56 @@
 ly_associate_package(PACKAGE_NAME cityhash-1.1-multiplatform                        TARGETS cityhash                    PACKAGE_HASH 0ace9e6f0b2438c5837510032d2d4109125845c0efd7d807f4561ec905512dd2)
 
 # platform-specific:
+if (NOT LY_USE_SYSTEM_EXPAT)
 ly_associate_package(PACKAGE_NAME expat-2.4.2-rev2-linux                            TARGETS expat                       PACKAGE_HASH 755369a919e744b9b3f835d1acc684f02e43987832ad4a1c0b6bbf884e6cd45b)
+else()
+    find_package(EXPAT REQUIRED)
+    if (NOT TARGET 3rdParty::expat)
+        add_library(3rdParty::expat ALIAS EXPAT::EXPAT)
+    endif()
+endif()
 ly_associate_package(PACKAGE_NAME assimp-5.4.3-rev3-linux                           TARGETS assimp                      PACKAGE_HASH 62ddd306d520b9b9ac6f587927ff82a90fb1e9e81d7609d67984551da376cf98)
